  "interpretation": [
    "All four WIC child input hashes exactly match the fixture hashes used by the worker, GDI+, and jpeg-js comparisons; each fixture has JPEG SOF 4:2:0 sampling factors.",
    "WPF/WIC and GDI+ produced identical RGBA values for every selected ROI point in all four cases (4096 total point comparisons; maximum RGB difference 0). This is agreement between two Windows imaging paths, not proof that either output is JPEG ground truth.",
    "The worker and pinned jpeg-js outputs matched byte-for-byte over the full 16 MP RGBA image in each single sample. Against WPF/WIC, the worker had 900/1024, 1000/1024, 1008/1024, and 768/1024 ROI pixels above 8, with maxima 70, 120, 136, and 147; these equal the worker-vs-GDI+ diagnostic counts.",
    "The evidence is consistent with different chroma reconstruction/phase behavior between the Chromium/Electron path and the Windows imaging paths. It does not establish which decoder is correct, generalize to the whole image, or close the JPEG fidelity gate.",
    "Each fixture/ROI uses one worker sample and was deliberately selected from prior mismatch investigation. The reporting tolerance is calibrated only for 4:4:4; all 4:2:0 comparisons remain diagnostic.",
    "WPF/WIC decoded only the selected CopyPixels rectangle in a fresh hidden STA PowerShell process. This is not a production WIC utilityProcess integration or a WIC latency/memory measurement. No system clipboard, input, foreground app, or installed application was used."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "WPF/WIC and GDI+ are platform imaging implementations; this experiment does not supply a normative JPEG reference or prove independence of their codec internals.",
    "The worker-to-jpeg-js full-frame match is a compatibility differential because jpeg-js is not independent from the existing decoder path.",
    "The selected ROIs are not random samples and cannot estimate full-frame error rates; only one worker sample was run per case.",
    "No production decoder code, user data, P15 path, system clipboard, physical input, foreground app, or installed/published application package was exercised. The existing Electron 40.10.2 development runtime was restored from a local archive whose SHA-256 matched the pinned package checksum; package manifests and lockfiles were unchanged."
  ]
